course: dictionary
lesson: 1313
title: Caesium, the metal that keeps time
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Caesium is a noun, a word for a thing. Look at the clues around it: «atomic clocks count the ticks of caesium atoms» tells you caesium is something tiny and important enough to count.
explain: Context also tells you what kind of thing a word means. «a radioactive metal» and «left in the soil» tell you caesium is a substance, not a place or a feeling. Swap your guess into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some words belong to a science group. Caesium is named in a list with sodium and potassium, so the sentence is pointing you to a family of metals. When context is not enough, a dictionary or a teacher can settle it.
fact: Caesium is a chemical element with the symbol Cs.
fact: Caesium is a soft, silvery-gold metal that reacts violently with water.
fact: Caesium is used in atomic clocks, the most accurate clocks there are.
fact: Today a second is measured by counting over 9 billion tiny ticks of caesium atoms.
fact: Caesium is in group 1 of the periodic table, with sodium and potassium.
exercise: What kind of word is caesium? | An adjective, a word that describes | An adverb, a word for how something is done | A verb, a doing word | *A noun, a word for a thing or substance
exercise: «Atomic clocks count the ticks of caesium atoms so exactly they'd lose less than a second in millions of years.» What are atomic clocks known for? | *Being the most accurate clocks there are | Being the loudest clocks | Telling the weather | Being made of wood
exercise: «The first accurate atomic clock was built in London in 1955.» Where was the first accurate atomic clock built? | *London | Glasgow | Germany | Paris
test: Caesium sits in a group of metals with sodium and potassium. What is that group called? | Noble gases | Halogens | Transition metals | *Alkali metals
test: «Mushrooms suck up caesium, a radioactive metal the explosion left in the soil.» What does radioactive mean? | Shiny and smooth | Full of water | Very cold to touch | *Giving off invisible energy rays from its atoms
exam: In «a quartz crystal in a watch wiggles 32,768 times a second, and atomic clocks count the ticks of caesium atoms so exactly», what is caesium's main job? | Making watches shiny | Cleaning the soil | Making mushrooms grow | *Keeping time very exactly
